44
00:06:03,400 --> 00:06:12,860
But it was Jamie Pennybaker from the University of Texas, Austin, who brought this idea to the scientific realm and really researched it.

45
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:22,580
And here is what he did. What he did was bring in participants and have them do the following.

46
00:06:23,140 --> 00:06:34,920
On four consecutive days that they came in, each day they would spend 15 minutes, that's all, 15 minutes times four, writing about their most difficult experiences.

47
00:06:35,740 --> 00:06:44,720
Now, they knew that no one would see it, or if they would see it, it would be without a name, completely confidential, so they were really able to treat it as their own journal.

48
00:06:47,710 --> 00:06:54,730
And here was the instructions that these participants got. It's a little long, but worth, I think, worth reading.

49
00:06:55,670 --> 00:07:01,530
Write continuously about the most upsetting or traumatic experience of your entire life.

50
00:07:02,350 --> 00:07:11,230
Don't worry about grammar, spelling or sentence structure. In your writing, I want you to discuss your deepest thoughts and feelings about the experience.

51
00:07:11,770 --> 00:07:19,070
You can write about anything you want. But whatever you choose, it should be something that has affected you very deeply.

52
00:07:19,830 --> 00:07:24,830
Ideally, it should be about something you have not talked about with others in detail.

53
00:07:25,210 --> 00:07:32,230
It is critical, however, that you let yourself go and touch those deepest emotions and thoughts that you have.

54
00:07:32,410 --> 00:07:38,510
In other words, write about what happened and how you felt about it and how you feel about it now.

55
00:07:38,970 --> 00:07:45,470
Finally, you can write on different traumas during each session or the same one over the entire study.

56
00:07:45,930 --> 00:07:49,690
Your choice of trauma for each session is entirely up to you.

57
00:07:50,410 --> 00:07:59,330
Simple instructions, pretty straightforward. if you notice you see the ABCs in it so he says write about what happened which

58
00:07:59,330 --> 00:08:04,010
is the behavior essentially write about your deepest feelings your affect your

59
00:08:04,010 --> 00:08:11,970
emotions and write about your thought analyze it the ABCs in journaling so

60
00:08:11,970 --> 00:08:20,210
when he did this study initially and the results came in because one of the first things that he looked at was their anxiety levels when the results

